This directory contain files required for the translation
of RTIR interfaces.

po/rtir.pot is a template.

To start a new translation, copy the template to po/<lang>.po where <lang>
is your language, for example ru, pt, pt_BR or other.

Translation files only need to contain strings that are specific to RTIR.
Strings that also appear in RT core (for example "Owner" or "Status") are
translated by RT itself, because RT merges its own catalog with every
plugin catalog for the same language. Omit them from po/<lang>.po rather
than leaving them blank.

To regenerate po/rtir.pot and update the po files, run this from the top
of the RTIR checkout, with RTHOME pointing at an RT source checkout:

    devel/tools/rtir-message-catalog extract

It runs RT's extractor and then removes strings that RT core already
translates. See the documentation in the script for the other commands.

Some strings may be missing from the rtir.pot file.  This may happen if a
developer forgot to use loc function or /l mason component. Usually it's
easy to fix. Find the string in the source, wrap it into call to the
function or the component. You can find examples of using these all over the
code. Then update message catalogs using the directions above.

